  70:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Start, Reload, Stop, Capture, and Count Inputs
  71:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
  72:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \n
  73:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \b PWM
  74:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
  75:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Use this mode when an output square wave is needed with a specific 
  76:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * period and duty cycle, such as:
  77:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Creating arbitrary square wave outputs
  78:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Driving an LED (changing the brightness)
  79:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Driving Motors (dead time assertion available)
  80:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
  81:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * The PWM has the following features:
  82:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * 16- or 32-bit Counter
  83:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Two Programmable Period registers that can be swapped
  84:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Two Output Compare registers that can be swapped on overflow and/or 
  85:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * underflow
  86:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Left Aligned, Right Aligned, Center Aligned, and Asymmetric Aligned modes
  87:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Continuous or One Shot run modes
  88:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Pseudo Random mode
  89:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Two PWM outputs with Dead Time insertion, and programmable polarity
  90:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Interrupt and Output on Overflow, Underflow, or Compare 
  91:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Start, Reload, Stop, Swap (Capture), and Count Inputs
  92:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Multiple Components can be synchronized together for applications 
  93:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * such as three phase motor control
  94:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
  95:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \n
  96:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \b Quadrature \b Decoder
  97:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
  98:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * A quadrature decoder is used to decode the output of a quadrature encoder. 
  99:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * A quadrature encoder senses the position, velocity, and direction of 
 100:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * an object (for example a rotating axle, or a spinning mouse ball). 
 101:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * A quadrature decoder can also be used for precision measurement of speed, 
 102:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * acceleration, and position of a motor's rotor, or with a rotary switch to 
 103:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * determine user input. \n
 104:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * 
 105:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * The Quadrature Decoder has the following features:
 106:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * 16- or 32-bit Counter
 107:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Counter Resolution of x1, x2, and x4 the frequency of the phiA (Count) and 
 108:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * phiB (Start) inputs
 109:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * Index Input to determine absolute position
 110:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * A positive edge on phiA increments the counter when phiB is 0 and decrements
 111:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * the counter when phiB is 1
 112:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 113:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \section group_tcpwm_configuration Configuration Considerations
 114:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 115:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * For each mode, the TCPWM driver has a configuration structure, an Init 
 116:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * function, and an Enable function. 
 117:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 118:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Provide the configuration parameters in the appropriate structure (see
 119:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Counter \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_counter, PWM 
 120:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_pwm, or QuadDec 
 121:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_quaddec). 
 122:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Then call the appropriate Init function: 
 123:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_Counter_Init, \ref Cy_TCPWM_PWM_Init, or 
 124:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_QuadDec_Init. Provide the address of the filled structure as a 
 125:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * parameter. To enable the counter, call the appropriate Enable function: 
 126:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_Counter_Enable, \ref Cy_TCPWM_PWM_Enable, or 
ARM GAS  C:\Users\haoen\AppData\Local\Temp\ccMjLtpq.s 			page 7


 127:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_QuadDec_Enable).
 128:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 129:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * Many functions work with an individual counter. You can also manage multiple 
 130:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * counters simultaneously for certain functions. These are listed in the 
 131:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_functions_common 
 132:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * section of the TCPWM. You can enable, disable, or trigger (in various ways) 
 133:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * multiple counters simultaneously. For these functions you provide a bit field 
 134:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * representing each counter in the TCPWM you want to control. You can 
 135:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * represent the bit field as an ORed mask of each counter, like 
 136:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * ((1U << cntNumX) | (1U << cntNumX) | (1U << cntNumX)), where X is the counter 
 137:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * number from 0 to 31.
 138:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 139:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \note
 140:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * If none of the input terminals (start, reload(index)) are used, the 
 141:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * software event \ref Cy_TCPWM_TriggerStart or 
 142:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref Cy_TCPWM_TriggerReloadOrIndex must be called to start the counting.
 143:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * * If count input terminal is not used, the \ref CY_TCPWM_INPUT_LEVEL macro 
 144:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * should be set for the countInputMode parameter and the \ref CY_TCPWM_INPUT_1 
 145:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * macro should be set for the countInput parameter in the configuration 
 146:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * structure of the appropriate mode(Counter 
 147:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_counter, PWM 
 148:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_pwm, or QuadDec 
 149:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \ref group_tcpwm_data_structures_quaddec).
 150:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** *
 151:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * \subsection group_tcpwm_pins Assign and Configure Pins
 152:Generated_Source\PSoC6\pdl\drivers/peripheral/tcpwm/cy_tcpwm.h **** * The dedicated TCPWM pins can be used. The HSIOM register must be configured to
